; A near-miss on a digit-leading set reports `not_member`, not
; `wrong_underlying`. Once a kind declares such a member the slot genuinely
; accepts unit-bearing numbers, so the useful report is "which ones are
; allowed" rather than "a number is not a symbol".
;
; Three ways to miss, one diagnostic each:
;
;   * `4d` — right unit, undeclared magnitude.
;   * `2b` — declared magnitude, wrong unit. The unit is part of the
;     identity, not decoration.
;   * `sphere` — an ordinary symbol that is not a member. The symbol path
;     is unchanged by any of this.
(plugin :name gpu :version "1.0.0" :sjon "1.3"
  (value-kind :name texture-dimension :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [1d 2d 3d]))
  (form :name texture (key :name dimension :type texture-dimension)))

(texture :dimension 4d)
(texture :dimension 2b)
(texture :dimension sphere)
